Lab 2: Install OpenShift Service Mesh
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Install and configure OpenShift Service Mesh operators using the Operator Lifecycle Manager (OLM) • Create and configure a Service Mesh Control Plane (SMCP) for managing microservices • Verify the successful installation of OpenShift Service Mesh using both the OpenShift CLI and Web Console • Understand the core components of Istio-based service mesh architecture • Troubleshoot common installation issues and validate service mesh functionality

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

• Basic understanding of Kubernetes and OpenShift concepts • Familiarity with microservices architecture principles • Knowledge of YAML configuration files • Experience with command-line interface operations • Understanding of container orchestration fundamentals • Access to OpenShift Container Platform 4.10 or later • Cluster administrator privileges on the OpenShift cluster

Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines
Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines with OpenShift Container Platform already installed. Simply click Start Lab to access your dedicated environment. No need to build your own virtual machine or install OpenShift from scratch.

Your lab environment includes: • OpenShift Container Platform 4.12 or later • Pre-configured cluster with administrative access • OpenShift CLI (oc) tool installed and configured • Web browser access to OpenShift Web Console

Task 1: Install Service Mesh Operators via Operator Lifecycle Manager
Subtask 1.1: Access the OpenShift Web Console
Open your web browser and navigate to the OpenShift Web Console URL provided in your lab environment
Log in using the administrator credentials provided
Verify you have cluster administrator privileges by checking the top-right corner shows your admin user
Subtask 1.2: Install the Elasticsearch Operator
The OpenShift Service Mesh requires the Elasticsearch Operator for distributed tracing functionality.

In the OpenShift Web Console, navigate to Operators → OperatorHub
In the search box, type Elasticsearch
Click on the OpenShift Elasticsearch Operator tile
Click Install
Configure the installation settings:
Installation Mode: All namespaces on the cluster
Installed Namespace: openshift-operators-redhat
Update Channel: stable
Approval Strategy: Automatic
Click Install to begin the installation
Wait for the operator status to show Succeeded
