Task 2: Set up SMCP (Service Mesh Control Plane)
Subtask 2.1: Create the Service Mesh Control Plane Namespace
Create a dedicated namespace for the service mesh control plane:
oc new-project istio-system
Verify the namespace was created:
oc get projects | grep istio-system
Subtask 2.2: Create the Service Mesh Control Plane Configuration
Create a YAML file for the Service Mesh Control Plane configuration:
cat > smcp-basic.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: maistra.io/v2
kind: ServiceMeshControlPlane
metadata:
  name: basic
  namespace: istio-system
spec:
  version: v2.4
  tracing:
    type: Jaeger
    sampling: 10000
  addons:
    jaeger:
      name: jaeger
      install:
        storage:
          type: Memory
    kiali:
      name: kiali
      enabled: true
      install:
        dashboard:
          viewOnly: false
    grafana:
      name: grafana
      enabled: true
  policy:
    type: Istiod
  telemetry:
    type: Istiod
  security:
    dataPlane:
      mtls: true
    controlPlane:
      mtls: true
  gateways:
    ClusterIngress:
      enabled: true
      runtime:
        deployment:
          autoScaling:
            enabled: false
        container:
          resources:
            requests:
              cpu: 10m
              memory: 128Mi
            limits:
              cpu: 100m
              memory: 128Mi
    ClusterEgress:
      enabled: false
EOF
Apply the Service Mesh Control Plane configuration:
oc apply -f smcp-basic.yaml
Monitor the installation progress:
oc get smcp -n istio-system
Wait for the SMCP status to show ComponentsReady:
oc get smcp basic -n istio-system -o jsonpath='{.status.conditions[?(@.type=="Ready")].status}'
Subtask 2.3: Create a Service Mesh Member Roll
The Service Mesh Member Roll defines which namespaces are part of the service mesh.

Create a Service Mesh Member Roll configuration:
cat > smmr-default.yaml << 'EOF'
apiVersion: maistra.io/v1
kind: ServiceMeshMemberRoll
metadata:
  name: default
  namespace: istio-system
spec:
  members:
  - bookinfo
  - production
  - testing
EOF
Apply the Service Mesh Member Roll:
oc apply -f smmr-default.yaml
Verify the member roll was created:
oc get smmr -n istio-system
Subtask 2.4: Verify Control Plane Components
Check all control plane pods are running:
oc get pods -n istio-system
Verify the following components are present and running:

istiod (Istio control plane)
istio-proxy (sidecar injector)
jaeger (distributed tracing)
kiali (service mesh observability)
grafana (metrics visualization)
Check the status of each component:

oc get pods -n istio-system -o wide
